      "hints": [
        "Tangency requires $\\Delta = (3k + 1)^2 = 0 \\implies k = -\\frac{1}{3}$.",
        "Substitute $k = -\\frac{1}{3}$ to find contact point $\\left(\\frac{2}{3}, -\\frac{1}{9}\\right)$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "For the line to be a tangent to the curve, the discriminant must be zero:\n$$(3k + 1)^2 = 0 \\implies 3k + 1 = 0 \\implies k = -\\frac{1}{3}$$",
        "Substitute $k = -\\frac{1}{3}$ into the quadratic equation to find the $x$-coordinate of the point of tangency:\n$$2x^2 - \\left(3 - \\frac{1}{3}\\right)x + \\left(1 - \\frac{1}{9}\\right) = 0 \\implies 2x^2 - \\frac{8}{3}x + \\frac{8}{9} = 0$$\n$$18x^2 - 24x + 8 = 0 \\implies 2(9x^2 - 12x + 4) = 0 \\implies 2(3x - 2)^2 = 0 \\implies x = \\frac{2}{3}$$",
        "Find the corresponding $y$-coordinate:\n$$y = 2\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^2 - 3\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right) + 1 = 2\\left(\\frac{4}{9}\\right) - 2 + 1 = \\frac{8}{9} - 1 = -\\frac{1}{9}$$\n$$k = -\\frac{1}{3}, \\quad \\text{Point of contact: } \\left(\\frac{2}{3}, -\\frac{1}{9}\\right)$$"
      ],
